{'symbol': 'AXP', 'date': '2022-11-04 09:00:00', 'title': 'AMERICAN EXPRESS COMMITS OVER $5 MILLION TO HELP CITIES BUILD RESILIENCE TO FIGHT CLIMATE CHANGE', 'text': 'NEW YORK--(BUSINESS WIRE)--AHEAD OF THE UNITED NATIONS CLIMATE CHANGE CONFERENCE (COP27) TAKING PLACE NEXT WEEK IN EGYPT, AMERICAN EXPRESS (NYSE: AXP) IS PLEDGING MORE THAN $5 MILLION TO ORGANIZATIONS HELPING CITIES AND COASTAL COMMUNITIES BUILD RESILIENCE AGAINST FUTURE CLIMATE-RELATED EVENTS, INCLUDING OCEAN CONSERVANCY, URBAN SUSTAINABILITY DIRECTORS NETWORK, RESILIENT CITIES CATALYST, AND REGIONAL PLAN ASSOCIATION.'}